<title>LEBANON: Lebanon January public debt up 3.61 pct - Banks Assn.</title>
<headline>Lebanon January public debt up 3.61 pct - Banks Assn.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's January public debt rose 3.61 percent, according to figures issued by the Lebanese Banks Association on Friday.</p>
<p>The cumulative deficit of income to expenditure fell to 50 percent from 52 percent at the end of December, the association said.</p>
<p>The association issued the following details of Lebanon's public finances (billions of Lebanese pounds at end of period unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>				 Oct 96   Nov 96   Dec 96   Jan 97</p>
<p>Revenues (Cumulative)     2,748   3,041    3,532	250</p>
<p>monthly change		  287     293	491	250</p>
<p>Expenses (Cumulative)     5,998   6,550    7,288	504</p>
<p>Monthly change		1,061     552    7,288	504</p>
<p>Deficit (Cumulative)	3,250   3,509    3,756	254</p>
<p>Monthly change		  774     259	247	254</p>
<p>Ratio deficit to expenses  0.54    0.54     0.52	0.5</p>
<p>Monthly change		 0.04   (0.01)   (0.02)     n/a</p>
<p>Total debt		   18,279  19,172   19,952   20.732</p>
<p>Month change(%)		2.77    4.88     4.07     3.61</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057</p>
</text>
